              "file": "apps/komki_mediator/lib/komki_mediator/vorpruefung.ex",
              "line": 117,
              "description": "The untrusted source is `params.arguments` of every MCP `tools/call`, fetched raw (server.ex:55) and passed to Vorpruefung before any depth/size bound; the vendored anubis layer only requires arguments to be an open `:map` (anubis message.ex:58 \"arguments\" => :map; peri.ex:796 validates :map with a bare is_map check), so arbitrarily deep nested objects pass. On any schema violation the refusal PDR hashes the raw arguments with `JSON.canonical/1`, a non-tail-recursive encoder that recurses once per attacker-chosen nesting level and builds `pad(depth) = List.duplicate(\"  \", depth)` at every level (json.ex:598, 618), making both live heap and output binary Θ(depth²).",
              "exploit_scenario": "pi, the sandboxed agent that legitimately holds the bearer token and connects to the 0600 socket, POSTs a tools/call for any advertised tool (e.g. \"ping\") with arguments = {\"a\":{\"a\":{\"a\":… ~50,000 levels deep …}}}. The OTP json decoder is iterative (explicit stack, no depth cap) and Peri's :map leaves values unchecked, so the term reaches Vorpruefung.check; Params.check rejects it as an unknown field, and refused/5 then canonicalizes the raw nested map to bind the intent_hash — the quadratic encoder allocates ~8·depth² bytes of heap and never returns, taking the mediator and the machine's memory with it.",
              "preconditions": [
                "Attacker is a local same-uid process that can reach the 0600 mediator unix socket and holds the bearer token (pi, the MCP client, holds it by design; any second token-holding session also qualifies)",
                "Mediator running with any room/registry"
