        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-863",
          "ruleIndex": 1,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Offenlegungsfreigabe: refused GO is still written as approval — confidential parts leave the room after the human answers \"no\".\n\nThe human's GO confirmation result (`go?`) never reaches the answer file: `GoSteps.answer_offenlegung/3` calls `KomkiMediator.Go.answer_selection/3` unconditionally with the selected part IDs, and answer_selection encodes any non-empty valid selection as `{\"go\" => true}` — which the mediator's `Go.selection_answer/4` treats as the human's GO, proceeding to build the release and execute the disclosure. The mediator-side contract (encoded in apps/komki_mediator/test/komki_mediator/go_essenz_test.exs:73-75) requires a refusal to be sent as an empty selection.\n\nImpact: Confidentiality bypass of the system's central human-consent control. For Offenlegungsfreigabe requests (Szene 13, #423) — the highest-stakes egress, where fraktion-confidential content is disclosed to the ratsprojekte hub — an explicit refusal (\"n\", EOF, or a non-terminal stdin) still results in the selected parts being POSTed to the hub (`/connector/fakt_vorschlagen`), where they become visible to the Redaktion/Vorstand/nextcloud-betreiber/sicherung recipient circle. The CLI even reports \"0 von 1 Anfragen freigegeben\" while the disclosure executes, so the human has no indication it happened. The headless variant is worse: a piped/scripted `komki go` auto-grants the offenlegung with ALL parts, because `KomkiCli.Prompt.select` defaults to \"all\" without a terminal and the never-encoded refusal leaves `go: true` in the file — defeating the documented guarantee that \"ein Ja darf nur eine Person geben, nie ein Skript\" (prompt.ex:15-17). The simple Aktionsfreigabe path is unaffected: `answer_simple/3` correctly passes `go?` into `Go.answer/3`.\n\nExploit scenario: The sandboxed agent (whose tool calls are influenced by untrusted room/web content) calls rp_fakt_vorschlagen from the fraktion room with parts containing faction-internal content. The mediator's store gate denies with recipient_not_allowed and offers the Offenlegungsfreigabe; a request file appears and the mediator waits up to 120 s while the session listener heartbeat is fresh. The human opens the GO popup (GoWatcher) or runs `komki go`, presses Enter at the part selection (Enter = all), and then answers \"n\" at \"GO: Ich lege die ausgewählten Teile bewusst gegenüber dem Vorstand offen.\" The CLI writes {\"schema\":\"komki-go-answer/1\",\"go\":true,\"teile\":[all ids]}; the mediator reads go:true, builds the komki-release/2 from its own request, the engine permits, GoStand commits the nonce, and the connector POSTs the parts to the hub — exactly the disclosure the human just declined.\n\nPreconditions: ratsprojekte hub configured (ratsprojekte_socket in config.json) and a fraktion room whose Γ offers the offenlegungsfreigabe remedy; a pending Offenlegungsfreigabe request while `komki go` runs (mediator await window, listener heartbeat active); the human declines at the GO prompt after a valid part selection — or, for full automation, any non-interactive `komki go` invocation while the request is pending.\n\nRecommendation: Only write the selection answer when the human confirmed: on refusal call `Go.answer_selection(dir, request, [])` (which writes {\"go\" => false}), exactly as the mediator-side test helper models it (go_essenz_test.exs:73-75), or add a `go?` parameter to `Go.answer_selection/3` so the refusal is encoded inside the callee. Add a CLI test for the offenlegung refusal path — the existing go_steps_test.exs only covers the simple Aktionsfreigabe (\"Nein (Default): keine Freigabe\") and never exercises a kind: offenlegungsfreigabe request, which is why this went unnoticed.\n\nCWE-863. Severity HIGH, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "apps/komki_cli/lib/komki_cli/go_steps.ex",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 112,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "case Go.answer_selection(dir, request, ids || []) do"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "KomkiCli.GoSteps.answer_offenlegung/3 (entry: KomkiCli.GoSteps.run/2)",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "KomkiCli.GoSteps.answer_offenlegung/3 (entry: KomkiCli.GoSteps.run/2)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "claudeSecurityPlugin": {
