        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-863",
          "ruleIndex": 1,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Verify accepts a forged binding_condition premise with \"expression\": null, suppressing the mandated expression_mismatch for rule-less bindings.\n\nThe proof document is the untrusted input to the independent checker (CONTRACT § 5 requires verify to discard every forged tree). For a checked binding that has no rule entry for the proof's operation, registry_rule_expression/3 returns nil, and a forged premise carrying \"expression\": null compares equal to it at line 709, so the contract-mandated expression_mismatch finding (§ 5 step 8: \"Hat die Bindung keinen Eintrag fuer die Regel, feuert ebenfalls expression_mismatch\") never fires; fact_refs and re-evaluation are then skipped (lines 718, 726) and verify returns result \"valid\" for a call that Derive.decide denies with missing_operation_rule.\n\nImpact: The anti-forgery guarantee of the independent proof checker is broken for the missing_operation_rule class: a hand-crafted komki-proof/1 tree verifies as sound (result: valid, exit 0) for a call the rule core denies. Any consumer that re-verifies presented or persisted decision records (the CLI `komki-policy verify --proof` command, or the mediator Gate-2 redaction control if the decision/proof ever arrives from outside the derive call) certifies a permit that the policy denies.\n\nExploit scenario: An attacker or tampered record supplies a proof file identical to a genuine admit/emit/store/transfer tree except that the binding_condition premise for a checked binding without the operation's rule is {\"binding\": b, \"expression\": null, \"fact_refs\": [], \"kind\": \"condition\", \"name\": \"binding_condition\", \"value\": true}. The premise passes input validation, fills the required slot (name/kind/binding all fit), and expression_check's nil == nil comparison suppresses the rejection. Verify.check returns {:ok, %{\"result\" => \"valid\", \"reasons\" => []}} although Derive.decide on the same registry/snapshot/intent returns deny with blocker missing_operation_rule.\n\nPreconditions: A caller presents a proof not produced in the same process (CLI `komki-policy verify` reads --proof from argv; the mediator currently passes only derive's own in-process proof, so live impact is on the CLI/audit surface); A checked binding (workspace.bindings for admit/emit, object labels for store/transfer) that has no operations entry for the proof's rule.\n\nRecommendation: In condition_reasons/3, fire the finding unconditionally when registry_expr is nil (e.g. `if is_nil(registry_expr) or premise[\"expression\"] != registry_expr -> reason(\"expression_mismatch\", ...)`), matching CONTRACT § 5 step 8, and reject non-boolean/non-map values for the premise's \"expression\" field during validate_proof so a null payload cannot impersonate the registry AST.\n\nCWE-863. Severity MEDIUM, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "apps/komki_policy/lib/komki_policy/verify.ex",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 709,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "    if premise[\"expression\"] != registry_expr,"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "KomkiPolicy.Verify.expression_check/3",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "KomkiPolicy.Verify.expression_check/3"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "claudeSecurityPlugin": {
              "id": "F5",
