              "file": "apps/komki_policy/lib/komki_policy/verify.ex",
              "line": 709,
              "description": "The proof document is the untrusted input to the independent checker (CONTRACT § 5 requires verify to discard every forged tree). For a checked binding that has no rule entry for the proof's operation, registry_rule_expression/3 returns nil, and a forged premise carrying \"expression\": null compares equal to it at line 709, so the contract-mandated expression_mismatch finding (§ 5 step 8: \"Hat die Bindung keinen Eintrag fuer die Regel, feuert ebenfalls expression_mismatch\") never fires; fact_refs and re-evaluation are then skipped (lines 718, 726) and verify returns result \"valid\" for a call that Derive.decide denies with missing_operation_rule.",
              "exploit_scenario": "An attacker or tampered record supplies a proof file identical to a genuine admit/emit/store/transfer tree except that the binding_condition premise for a checked binding without the operation's rule is {\"binding\": b, \"expression\": null, \"fact_refs\": [], \"kind\": \"condition\", \"name\": \"binding_condition\", \"value\": true}. The premise passes input validation, fills the required slot (name/kind/binding all fit), and expression_check's nil == nil comparison suppresses the rejection. Verify.check returns {:ok, %{\"result\" => \"valid\", \"reasons\" => []}} although Derive.decide on the same registry/snapshot/intent returns deny with blocker missing_operation_rule.",
              "preconditions": [
                "A caller presents a proof not produced in the same process (CLI `komki-policy verify` reads --proof from argv; the mediator currently passes only derive's own in-process proof, so live impact is on the CLI/audit surface)",
                "A checked binding (workspace.bindings for admit/emit, object labels for store/transfer) that has no operations entry for the proof's rule"
              ],
              "category": "Incorrect Authorization",
              "severity": "MEDIUM",
              "confidence": "high",
              "recommendation": "In condition_reasons/3, fire the finding unconditionally when registry_expr is nil (e.g. `if is_nil(registry_expr) or premise[\"expression\"] != registry_expr -> reason(\"expression_mismatch\", ...)`), matching CONTRACT § 5 step 8, and reject non-boolean/non-map values for the premise's \"expression\" field during validate_proof so a null payload cannot impersonate the registry AST.",
              "cwe_id": "CWE-863",
              "snippet": "    if premise[\"expression\"] != registry_expr,",
