        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-1333",
          "ruleIndex": 3,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Quadratic-backtracking regex in Note.heading/1 lets crafted vault notes burn CPU on every search and read (ReDoS).\n\nVault note content is untrusted input (human/Obsidian/sync-authored files, or the agent's own write_test body), and Note.parse feeds it into a regex whose lazy group (.+?) and greedy space run ([ \t]*) can both match the same characters before the $ anchor — a line `# a` + long space run + `x` makes PCRE re-scan the space run at every lazy length, O(S²/2) match calls, bounded only by PCRE's default match_limit (10,000,000, verified in the installed OTP's re.erl docs). Elixir's Regex.run passes no report_errors, so the limit hit yields nomatch — the cost is paid as ~10^7 PCRE match calls of CPU per parse with no crash, per note, on every read and every search.\n\nImpact: Availability only, but persistent and shared: vault_search parses every shape-labeled note in the vault on every call (komki_connector_vault.ex:59-73, visible/2 -> load -> Note.parse) before the mediator's Gate 2 filters anything, so each crafted note adds up to the full PCRE match budget (10^7 internal match calls — wall-clock estimated at roughly 0.1-0.5 s per note per call, derived from documented PCRE semantics, not measured) to every vault_search in every room and to every read of the note. A few dozen to ~100 planted notes (each ~20 KB, one write_test call apiece) push the operation past the mediator's 15 s Sidecar.Client timeout, making vault_search return upstream-timeout for all rooms until the notes are found and removed; abandoned searches keep burning in the connector (one request per connection), so repeated calls also pin the host's CPU cores.\n\nExploit scenario: The prompt-injected agent (this system's declared adversary, CONTRACT.md §1) in any room where vault_write_test is permitted issues a few dozen write calls with title \"\\u0001\" and body \"# a\" <> String.duplicate(\" \", 19995) <> \"x\" (within the 20,000-char cap). The notes land in <vault>/komki-test with valid frontmatter labels; because the control-char title decodes to empty, every later parse runs the quadratic heading regex over the crafted line and burns the full PCRE match budget. Every subsequent vault_search in every room times out, disabling vault search (and making vault_read of the planted notes slow) until someone deletes the notes by hand. The identical burn needs no agent write access at all: any file synced/collaborated into the vault without a frontmatter title and with a pathological `# `-line triggers it, and human-authored files may be up to the 1 MiB size cap instead of 20 KB.\n\nPreconditions: A room that permits vault_write_test (the tool's normal configuration) for the agent route — or attacker-influenced vault file content (Obsidian sync/collaboration/plugin) for the external route, which needs no write permission; The crafted note carries a shape-valid komki_labels entry and no usable frontmatter title; The note body's first `# `-heading line consists of a long run of spaces/tabs terminated by a non-space character.\n\nRecommendation: Restructure the title extraction so the regex has no lazy-group/greedy-run ambiguity: match the raw line with ~r/^# (.+)$/m and trim trailing spaces/tabs with String.trim_trailing in Elixir (or limit the heading scan to the first N bytes/lines of the body). Additionally pass an explicit small match_limit to :re.run for these content-side regexes, and make visible/2 (komki_connector_vault.ex:115) tolerate per-note failures (rescue or match_limit budget per note) so one pathological note cannot dominate every search op.\n\nCWE-1333. Severity MEDIUM, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "apps/komki_connector_vault/lib/komki_connector_vault/note.ex",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 76,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "case Regex.run(~r/^# +(.+?)[ \\t]*$/m, body) do"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "KomkiConnectorVault.Note.heading/1",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "KomkiConnectorVault.Note.heading/1"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
