        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-863",
          "ruleIndex": 1,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Verify does not bind a fact premise's asserted fact to its slot name, so a forged proof can verify the wrong fact and pass a denied call.\n\nThe required-set reconstruction discharges a premise slot by (name, kind) only (fits_slot?/expected_kind, verify.ex:502-526), but the predicate check then takes the fact to verify from the attacker-supplied \"fact\" field (line 579) without ever comparing it to the slot's name. A forged premise named \"audit_path_ready\" (or \"workspace_contract_valid\", \"has_operation_right\", ...) that asserts a different, true fact fills the required slot while checking that other fact's value, so a proof over a snapshot whose real premise fact is false (or whose workspace.valid is false, since the workspace check at line 581 is keyed on the claimed fact name, not the slot name) verifies as valid although Derive.decide denies with audit_path_not_ready / workspace_invalid / basis_right_false.\n\nImpact: A forged komki-proof/1 tree substitutes the premise payload of any basis-fact slot (including the workspace_contract_valid slot, bypassing the workspace_invalid denial) with a duplicate check of an already-true fact; the independent checker returns result: valid (exit 0) for a call the rule core denies. This defeats the manipulated-proof guarantee of CONTRACT § 8 (\"Manipulierte Beweise (alle von verify zu verwerfen)\") for the basis-fact and workspace-validity blocker classes on any consumer that verifies a presented proof (CLI verify; re-verification of externally sourced decision records).\n\nExploit scenario: Given an admit snapshot where audit_path_ready is false (all other facts true, recipients fine), Derive.decide denies with blocker audit_path_not_ready. The attacker copies the corresponding all-true permit tree and changes only the audit_path_ready premise's payload to {\"fact\": \"has_object_access_right\", \"kind\": \"fact\", \"name\": \"audit_path_ready\", \"source\": \"x\", \"source_kind\": \"administered\", \"value\": true}. The premise passes shape validation, discharges the audit_path_ready slot by name/kind, and fact_premise_finding checks has_object_access_right (true) instead of audit_path_ready (false); every other premise verifies genuinely, so Verify.check returns {\"result\": \"valid\", \"reasons\": []}. The same substitution on the workspace_contract_valid slot bypasses a false workspace.valid.\n\nPreconditions: A caller presents a proof not produced in the same process (CLI `komki-policy verify` reads --proof from argv; the mediator currently passes only derive's own in-process proof); A snapshot whose denied premise is a basis fact or workspace validity while at least one other fact is true (the redirected payload).\n\nRecommendation: In fact_premise_finding/2 (or fact_premise_reasons/2), require premise[\"name\"] == premise[\"fact\"] for kind \"fact\" premises per the CONTRACT § 2.5 shape, so a required slot can only be discharged by the fact it names; treat a mismatch as an unknown_premise/expression-class structural finding rather than verifying the claimed fact.\n\nCWE-863. Severity MEDIUM, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "apps/komki_policy/lib/komki_policy/verify.ex",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 579,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "    fact_name = Map.fetch!(premise, \"fact\")"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "KomkiPolicy.Verify.fact_premise_finding/2",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "KomkiPolicy.Verify.fact_premise_finding/2"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
