        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-863",
          "ruleIndex": 1,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Verify accepts permit proofs whose fact/object_check premises claim false: no 'all premises yield true' enforcement on the permit conclusion.\n\nUntrusted proof terms (CLI --proof file, or any caller-supplied term) enter Verify.check, whose documented purpose is to reject forged permit trees (CONTRACT § 5: 'glaubt kein permit', step 9: 'permit ist nur gültig, wenn alle neu geprüften Prämissen true ergeben'). The fact-premise check only compares the claimed value against the snapshot and never requires the re-checked premise to be true, and quarantine_reasons ignores the object_check premise's claimed value entirely — so a proof with conclusion \"permit\" whose premises honestly claim value:false against a deny-snapshot produces no finding and verifies as valid.\n\nImpact: The independent derivation checker — the component's anti-forgery control for permit records — certifies fabricated permits. An actor can present a komki-proof/1 that 'proves' an engine-approved permit for a call the rule core denies (basis_right_false, workspace_invalid, unproven-observer indeterminate), and any party relying on Verify.check or `komki-policy verify` (exit 0 = valid) to audit or re-certify decisions accepts the fabricated authorization record.\n\nExploit scenario: Against the engine's own fixture case_deny_no_basis (public room, has_operation_right: false — Derive returns deny/blocker basis_right_false): craft a komki-proof/1 with checked_label [], conclusion \"permit\", the has_operation_right fact premise claiming \"value\": false (mirroring the snapshot), all other premises faithful. Verify.check on the identical registry/snapshot/intent returns {\"result\" => \"valid\"}. The same works with workspace_contract_valid claiming false on a snapshot with workspace.valid false, and with a not_quarantine premise claiming false.\n\nPreconditions: A relying party runs Verify.check (library or `komki-policy verify` CLI) on a proof that did not originate in-process from Derive — e.g. an auditor, external integrator, or the planned historical-audit flow (CONTRACT Anhang F). The in-repo mediator callers (gate.ex:271, connector_gate.ex:924) only feed engine-generated proofs, which bounds direct exploitability today.\n\nRecommendation: In predicate_reasons, require premise[\"value\"] == true for every premise of a permit tree and fire conclusion_mismatch whenever a re-checked fact premise's snapshot value is not true (CONTRACT § 5 step 9); also compare the object_check premise's claimed value with the recomputed classification verdict instead of ignoring it.\n\nCWE-863. Severity MEDIUM, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "apps/komki_policy/lib/komki_policy/verify.ex",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 591,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "entry -> mismatch_if(premise[\"value\"] != Map.fetch!(entry, \"value\"), \"fact_value_mismatch\")"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "fact_entry_finding/3",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "fact_entry_finding/3"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "claudeSecurityPlugin": {
