              "impact": "The independent derivation checker — the component's anti-forgery control for permit records — certifies fabricated permits. An actor can present a komki-proof/1 that 'proves' an engine-approved permit for a call the rule core denies (basis_right_false, workspace_invalid, unproven-observer indeterminate), and any party relying on Verify.check or `komki-policy verify` (exit 0 = valid) to audit or re-certify decisions accepts the fabricated authorization record.",
              "file": "apps/komki_policy/lib/komki_policy/verify.ex",
              "line": 591,
              "description": "Untrusted proof terms (CLI --proof file, or any caller-supplied term) enter Verify.check, whose documented purpose is to reject forged permit trees (CONTRACT § 5: 'glaubt kein permit', step 9: 'permit ist nur gültig, wenn alle neu geprüften Prämissen true ergeben'). The fact-premise check only compares the claimed value against the snapshot and never requires the re-checked premise to be true, and quarantine_reasons ignores the object_check premise's claimed value entirely — so a proof with conclusion \"permit\" whose premises honestly claim value:false against a deny-snapshot produces no finding and verifies as valid.",
              "exploit_scenario": "Against the engine's own fixture case_deny_no_basis (public room, has_operation_right: false — Derive returns deny/blocker basis_right_false): craft a komki-proof/1 with checked_label [], conclusion \"permit\", the has_operation_right fact premise claiming \"value\": false (mirroring the snapshot), all other premises faithful. Verify.check on the identical registry/snapshot/intent returns {\"result\" => \"valid\"}. The same works with workspace_contract_valid claiming false on a snapshot with workspace.valid false, and with a not_quarantine premise claiming false.",
