        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-203",
          "ruleIndex": 5,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "admit_document is an existence-and-label oracle for non-admissible room documents (distinct deny vs unknown-object responses).\n\nThe agent-facing admit path resolves the requested document_id against room.json (Room.object_for_call) and answers a registered-but-blocked document with a full deny + remedies (whose neuer_raum.required_bindings is the document's λ(x), KomkiPolicy.Remedies:422-423), while an unregistered id yields a distinct error \"unbekanntes Objekt\" — the response discrepancy lets the untrusted model probe and enumerate exactly the confidential-document population that list_documents deliberately conceals (gate.ex:88-91: \"sonst verriete die Liste die Existenz vertraulicher Dokumente\").\n\nImpact: Confidentiality: a probing model learns which confidential documents exist in the room, their exact labels and the bindings needed to admit them. No document content leaks (deny is enforced before the connector read), but the disclosure defeats the concealment invariant the codebase itself states for list_documents and vault search (\"otherwise 'deny' versus 'permit, 0 hits' would be an existence oracle\", connector_gate.ex:877).\n\nExploit scenario: A prompt-injected agent iterates admit_document over guessable kebab-case slugs (document ids are slugified file names; the shipped demo set is literally doc-vertraulich). Each probe maps to deny-with-λ(x) (exists, blocked, label disclosed) or error-unbekanntes-Objekt (absent), reconstructing the hidden-document list and then nudging the user toward a room or transformation that would admit it.\n\nPreconditions: A room with workspace_bindings (the normal case; without it every call errors uniformly); The model actively probes candidate document ids — the shipped default room already contains a registered, non-admissible doc-vertraulich as a live target.\n\nRecommendation: Make the response for a type-\"document\" object that exists but is not admissible indistinguishable from the unknown-object response (or route both through the same generic deny shape), and withhold λ(x) from remedies on the admit path for objects the caller has no admissible way to know. Mirror the vault-search treatment (drop silently, no distinguishable outcome).\n\nCWE-204. Severity MEDIUM, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "apps/komki_mediator/lib/komki_mediator/gate.ex",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 396,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "      \"detail\" => \"unbekanntes Objekt: \" <> Kernel.inspect(object_id)"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "KomkiMediator.Gate.unknown_object/4",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "KomkiMediator.Gate.unknown_object/4"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
