        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-276",
          "ruleIndex": 6,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "GO and mediator state directories get default permissions: denied-output previews, confidential room documents and PDR journal readable by other local users.\n\nThe untrusted source is any other local (different-uid) user on the host; the sink is the GO request file written 0644 into the 0755 directory that `Go.await/2` creates with bare `File.mkdir_p!` — that file holds the full rendered params of the output the policy engine just denied as too confidential to leave the room (connector_gate.ex:336 \"params\" => call.params). Nothing in the mediator or komki_cli ever restricts `<base>/mediator` or its go/, journal/, documents/ subdirectories (only run/, connectors/ and denials/ are chmod'd 0700), so the mediator's own documented boundary — go.ex:10-12 \"pi kann dort weder lesen noch schreiben, also auch kein GO ausstellen\" — is enforced for pi by seatbelt but for everyone else only by the home directory's 0700, which this code neither sets nor checks.\n\nImpact: Confidentiality of the exact content the mediation exists to contain: the complete text of outputs the engine refused to release (GO request previews), confidential room documents (doc-vertraulich class), the append-only PDR audit journal, and the consumed-GO nonce ledger (stand.json). Integrity of GO approvals is not affected (0755 dirs deny other-uid writes).\n\nExploit scenario: On a shared machine an instance runs with a short base outside the home (e.g. KOMKI_HOME=/private/tmp/komki-test, the location komki itself suggests when the socket path exceeds the 103-byte macOS limit). The model proposes a fact built from internal fraktion material; the engine denies it and opens a GO window; `Go.await` writes the entire proposal text to /private/tmp/komki-test/mediator/go/<hash>.request.json with mode 0644. Any other local user reads it — and equally the confidential room documents under mediator/documents/ and the PDR journal — without any token, socket or seatbelt ever being in the way.\n\nPreconditions: Multi-user host with other unprivileged local accounts; Base directory not shielded by a 0700 home — custom KOMKI_HOME/--base (the CLI recommends /private/tmp for the socket path limit) or weakened home permissions; A GO window open or provisioned room documents/journal present at the time of the read.\n\nRecommendation: At creation, restrict the mediator's state like its siblings: chmod 0700 for `<base>/mediator`, `mediator/go`, `mediator/journal` and `mediator/documents` (Go.await go.ex:108, GoStand.init, Journal init journal.ex:171, Templates.provision!/write_templates, and KomkiCli.Connectors.ensure_run_dirs! for documents_dir), and chmod 0600 for the files written into them — GO request/answer files, stand.json, room.json/registry.json, room documents and pdr.jsonl — mirroring the 0700/0600 treatment `komki up` already applies to run/, the connectors dir and the token.\n\nCWE-276. Severity MEDIUM, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "apps/komki_mediator/lib/komki_mediator/go.ex",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 108,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "File.mkdir_p!(dir)"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "KomkiMediator.Go.await/2",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "KomkiMediator.Go.await/2"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "claudeSecurityPlugin": {
              "id": "F13",
              "title": "GO and mediator state directories get default permissions: denied-output previews, confidential room documents and PDR journal readable by other local users",
              "impact": "Confidentiality of the exact content the mediation exists to contain: the complete text of outputs the engine refused to release (GO request previews), confidential room documents (doc-vertraulich class), the append-only PDR audit journal, and the consumed-GO nonce ledger (stand.json). Integrity of GO approvals is not affected (0755 dirs deny other-uid writes).",
              "file": "apps/komki_mediator/lib/komki_mediator/go.ex",
              "line": 108,
              "description": "The untrusted source is any other local (different-uid) user on the host; the sink is the GO request file written 0644 into the 0755 directory that `Go.await/2` creates with bare `File.mkdir_p!` — that file holds the full rendered params of the output the policy engine just denied as too confidential to leave the room (connector_gate.ex:336 \"params\" => call.params). Nothing in the mediator or komki_cli ever restricts `<base>/mediator` or its go/, journal/, documents/ subdirectories (only run/, connectors/ and denials/ are chmod'd 0700), so the mediator's own documented boundary — go.ex:10-12 \"pi kann dort weder lesen noch schreiben, also auch kein GO ausstellen\" — is enforced for pi by seatbelt but for everyone else only by the home directory's 0700, which this code neither sets nor checks.",
              "exploit_scenario": "On a shared machine an instance runs with a short base outside the home (e.g. KOMKI_HOME=/private/tmp/komki-test, the location komki itself suggests when the socket path exceeds the 103-byte macOS limit). The model proposes a fact built from internal fraktion material; the engine denies it and opens a GO window; `Go.await` writes the entire proposal text to /private/tmp/komki-test/mediator/go/<hash>.request.json with mode 0644. Any other local user reads it — and equally the confidential room documents under mediator/documents/ and the PDR journal — without any token, socket or seatbelt ever being in the way.",
              "preconditions": [
                "Multi-user host with other unprivileged local accounts",
                "Base directory not shielded by a 0700 home — custom KOMKI_HOME/--base (the CLI recommends /private/tmp for the socket path limit) or weakened home permissions",
                "A GO window open or provisioned room documents/journal present at the time of the read"
              ],
              "category": "Incorrect Default Permissions",
              "severity": "MEDIUM",
              "confidence": "medium",
              "recommendation": "At creation, restrict the mediator's state like its siblings: chmod 0700 for `<base>/mediator`, `mediator/go`, `mediator/journal` and `mediator/documents` (Go.await go.ex:108, GoStand.init, Journal init journal.ex:171, Templates.provision!/write_templates, and KomkiCli.Connectors.ensure_run_dirs! for documents_dir), and chmod 0600 for the files written into them — GO request/answer files, stand.json, room.json/registry.json, room documents and pdr.jsonl — mirroring the 0700/0600 treatment `komki up` already applies to run/, the connectors dir and the token.",
              "cwe_id": "CWE-276",
              "snippet": "File.mkdir_p!(dir)",
              "symbol": "KomkiMediator.Go.await/2",
              "declared_line": 108,
              "claudeSecurityPluginFindingId": "v3:88e2007ba34e0650732327cbc01c7bc0cbd0fd9e157e812e4982df6053607910",
              "verification": {
                "panel": {
                  "true": 3,
                  "false": 0,
                  "voters": 3
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-203",
          "ruleIndex": 5,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Vault Gate 2 answers with an observationally distinct 'redacted label_not_in_gamma' state, giving the model an existence oracle over vault notes outside the room's label governance.\n\nThe vault connector deliberately returns confidential and public notes alike (form-valid labels pass, komki_connector_vault.ex:8-11,137-140) and leaves filtering to the mediator; but for a note whose labels are not Γ bindings the mediator redacts with a distinctive reason while a nonexistent note yields connector not-found — two distinguishable answers over attacker-chosen note paths and search keywords.\n\nImpact: Confidentiality, metadata only: the untrusted model learns which note paths/keywords exist in the user's vault with labels outside the registry's bindings — content itself is always withheld. This is the exact existence-oracle class the design engineered away for search (connector_gate.ex:873-877, labbook L-109); the non-Γ case reintroduces it for both single reads and, worse, whole-answer redaction on search.\n\nExploit scenario: In a room where vault tools are usable (emit/transfer bind only the request, never the note's labels, so they pass), the model probes vault_read(\"bewerbungen/2026.md\") or runs vault_search(\"Diagnose\"). not-found/empty-results means no such note; `admitted: \"redacted\"`, reason \"Labels der Notiz ausserhalb von Γ\" means a note matching that path or keyword exists but lies outside Γ — enumeration of private vault content the room was never meant to see, including keyword-based probing via the search redaction path (admit/5 checks all hits' labels before visible/3 filters, connector_gate.ex:845-847).\n\nPreconditions: vault connector enabled (vault_dir configured); room Γ/B_W permits vault read/search calls at all (the emit/transfer decisions pass); attacker is the authenticated MCP caller — which by design is the model.\n\nRecommendation: Make the withheld state observationally identical to not-found: resolve the note's labels against Γ before the connector reads content and answer with the same closed not-found error for non-Γ notes; and for search, silently drop non-Γ hits (the L-109 invariant) instead of redacting the entire answer, so hit counts and redaction state reveal nothing about notes outside the room's governance.\n\nCWE-203. Severity MEDIUM, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "apps/komki_mediator/lib/komki_mediator/connector_gate.ex",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
