        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-1333",
          "ruleIndex": 3,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Quadratic HTML-strip regex over unbounded upstream content enables CPU-exhaustion of the RIS connector.\n\nUntrusted source: the RIS HTTP response — every textblocks.content of guestagendaitems (and the raw content string when Base.decode64 fails, top.ex:76-81) — reaches the sink `String.replace(~r/<[^>]*>/, \" \")`, a backtracking-engine regex whose per-start cost is proportional to the remaining run of non-'>' bytes (O(n^2) on e.g. 1 MB of '<'). Neither the content size nor the number of textblocks is bounded anywhere, and the connector's 5 s/12 s budgets (api.ex:79) guard only the HTTP request, never the text processing that follows.\n\nImpact: Availability: the request-serving Task burns CPU far beyond the 15 s frame timeout (the caller gives up, the Task keeps spinning on the regex); repeatable per request since each connection spawns a fresh Task, so a hostile meeting list poisons every ris_search/ris_show call and accumulated processes pin the sidecar node's schedulers. No confidentiality or integrity impact; the op itself ends in 'internal'.\n\nExploit scenario: A hostile or compromised RIS (or a third party who can plant content in a public agenda item) serves guestagendaitems with many textblocks whose content is a huge run of '<' characters (or any invalid-base64 data, which falls to the raw-HTML branch). ris_show, or ris_search's automatic phase-2 text fetch, feeds each block to the regex; a single response with ~1000 such blocks (deliverable within the 5 s request timeout by a datacenter peer) keeps the serving process busy for minutes, long after the mediator answered upstream-timeout. With no match limit in force, a single 1 MB block alone would be quadratic (order hours).\n\nPreconditions: Upstream RIS response content is attacker-influenced: hostile/compromised risapi1.komuna.net, or planted text in a public agenda item (e.g. citizen petition) served by the real RIS; The agent calls search/show on a meeting whose agenda contains the payload (search phase 2 fetches pending TOP texts automatically, so no specific victim interaction is needed).\n\nRecommendation: Bound the work before it runs: cap accepted bytes per textblock and per response (also fixes the unbounded decode), re-check Api.remaining before each plain/1 call (the budget is already checked only before HTTP), and replace the regex strip with a single-pass linear scanner.\n\nCWE-1333. Severity MEDIUM, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "apps/komki_connector_ris/lib/komki_connector_ris/top.ex",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 84,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "|> String.replace(~r/<[^>]*>/, \" \")"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "KomkiConnectorRis.Top.plain/1",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "KomkiConnectorRis.Top.plain/1"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "claudeSecurityPlugin": {
