        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-862",
          "ruleIndex": 10,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "komki-tresor releases the ECDH shared secret to any caller; the Touch ID dialog text is caller-supplied, so the consent gate is forgeable.\n\n`agree` releases the ECDH shared secret (printed to stdout, main.swift:97) to any same-uid process after a user-presence check, and the only information the person sees to authorize the release — `localizedReason` — comes entirely from the caller's `--reason` argv (accepted at main.swift:92). Malware can read a ktv2 seal from the keychain (any same-uid process can, per the component's own model, secrets.ex:8-11), extract `key`/`eph`/`box`, invoke the genuine komki-tresor with komki's exact reason text, and after the user approves a prompt indistinguishable from a real `komki up` prompt, derive HKDF(salt=eph, info=\"ktv2\") and AES-GCM-decrypt the seal offline.\n\nImpact: Recovery of every sealed secret in plaintext — the Brave API key, the ratsprojekte-hub token, and (same helper via Ratsprojekte.Schluessel) the hub's SQLCipher database key — collapsing the seal scheme's confidentiality guarantee to one socially-engineered biometric approval.\n\nExploit scenario: Same-uid malware reads the seal for `brave-search-api` via `security find-generic-password -s brave-search-api -w`, base64-decodes `key`/`eph`/`box`, then runs `komki-tresor agree --reason \"komki startet den Connector web: Brave-Search-API-Key für die Websuche\"` piping `ref eph` on stdin, timed to a moment the user expects a Touch ID prompt (during `komki up`). The dialog shows the genuine binary and komki's own text; on approval the malware receives the shared secret and decrypts the seal.\n\nPreconditions: Attacker runs code as the same uid as the user; Victim approves one Touch ID / password prompt whose text the attacker authored.\n\nRecommendation: Do not let the caller author the consent basis: derive the dialog text from the request itself plus an unpredictable element (e.g., a per-agreement nonce that komki also logs so the user can cross-check), or verify the requesting process (code signature of the ancestor chain) before performing the agreement. Caller-supplied reason text is presentation, not authorization.\n\nCWE-862. Severity MEDIUM, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "apps/komki_cli/native/komki-tresor/main.swift",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 56,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  context.localizedReason = reason"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "agree(_ line: String, reason: String) -> String",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "agree(_ line: String, reason: String) -> String"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "claudeSecurityPlugin": {
