        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-1284",
          "ruleIndex": 11,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Request body over the 64 KiB cap hits an unhandled {:more, _} return and raises instead of answering 400.\n\nThe body of the caller's POST is the hub's only untrusted production input, and the hub's stated posture is to re-validate the connector's input itself; but Plug.Conn.read_body/2 with length: @max_body returns {:more, partial_body, conn} (not {:ok}/{:error}) for a body larger than 65 536 bytes (verified in apps/artifacts/deps/plug/lib/plug/conn.ex:1139-1182), and neither the with-head nor the else at http.ex:46-52 matches that shape, so the route raises WithClauseError and Bandit's pipeline rescue (apps/artifacts/deps/bandit/lib/bandit/pipeline.ex:57-66) answers 500 — the intended 400 validation and the anfragen.log entry are both skipped.\n\nImpact: No data is stored or leaked and the hub keeps serving (Bandit uses one process per connection), but an oversized request produces an unhandled exception (500) instead of the designed 400, and because log_and_respond/4 never runs the request is missing from anfragen.log, so the Redaktion's Connector-Anfragen count under-reports.\n\nExploit scenario: A buggy or hostile connector — the only legitimate token holder, and exactly the party the hub says it does not blindly trust (\"Der Hub vertraut dem Connector nicht blind\", http.ex:126-129) — sends a proposal body of 65 537 bytes; every such request crashes the handler instead of being rejected by validation.\n\nPreconditions: Ability to connect to <dir>/hub.sock (0600, same uid); Valid KOMKI_HUB_TOKEN bearer token; POST /connector/fakt_vorschlagen with a body larger than 65 536 bytes (the legitimate connector's manifest-bounded requests max out around 13 KiB, so the path is only hit by a misbehaving or token-stealing caller).\n\nRecommendation: Handle the oversized case explicitly: match {:more, _partial, conn} in the else (or read in a loop with a running total cap) and answer 400 with a fixed detail text like the other validation failures, so every request class ends in a logged, closed answer.\n\nCWE-1284. Severity LOW, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
