        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-400",
          "ruleIndex": 8,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Upstream response body is buffered and JSON-decoded with no size or depth limit.\n\nUntrusted source: the entire upstream HTTP response body. :httpc buffers it with no limit (body_format: :binary, http.ex:83) and the sink `{:ok, :json.decode(body)}` decodes it with no byte cap and no nesting-depth cap; the protocol's only size limit (Sidecar.Frame 1 MiB) applies to socket frames and the reply, never to upstream bodies, and api.ex:79 bounds the request only in time.\n\nImpact: Availability: memory exhaustion of the connector's BEAM node — the body and its decoded terms (several times larger with nested structures) are held per request while the serving Task outlives the caller's timeout; concurrent requests multiply the pressure toward system-wide OOM. No confidentiality or integrity impact.\n\nExploit scenario: The upstream RIS answers a guestmeetings/guestagendaitems GET with a body of tens to hundreds of MB (or a modest body with deeply nested arrays) delivered within the 5 s request timeout; :httpc buffers it whole and :json.decode materializes it as terms. The mediator's 15 s timeout abandons the call but does not stop the connector's Task, which keeps allocating; a hostile meeting window makes every search fetch such payloads again.\n\nPreconditions: Hostile or compromised risapi1.komuna.net (or a hostile host passed via --base-url) able to push a multi-hundred-MB or deeply nested JSON body within the 5 s per-request timeout.\n\nRecommendation: Enforce a maximum accepted body size (abort above a fixed byte budget, or stream with a cap) and a JSON nesting-depth limit before decoding; cap the sizes of individual fields (textblocks.content) that later stages process.\n\nCWE-400. Severity LOW, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "apps/komki_connector_ris/lib/komki_connector_ris/http.ex",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 96,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "{:ok, :json.decode(body)}"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "KomkiConnectorRis.Http.decode/1",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "KomkiConnectorRis.Http.decode/1"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "claudeSecurityPlugin": {
              "id": "F29",
              "title": "Upstream response body is buffered and JSON-decoded with no size or depth limit",
              "impact": "Availability: memory exhaustion of the connector's BEAM node — the body and its decoded terms (several times larger with nested structures) are held per request while the serving Task outlives the caller's timeout; concurrent requests multiply the pressure toward system-wide OOM. No confidentiality or integrity impact.",
              "file": "apps/komki_connector_ris/lib/komki_connector_ris/http.ex",
              "line": 96,
              "description": "Untrusted source: the entire upstream HTTP response body. :httpc buffers it with no limit (body_format: :binary, http.ex:83) and the sink `{:ok, :json.decode(body)}` decodes it with no byte cap and no nesting-depth cap; the protocol's only size limit (Sidecar.Frame 1 MiB) applies to socket frames and the reply, never to upstream bodies, and api.ex:79 bounds the request only in time.",
              "exploit_scenario": "The upstream RIS answers a guestmeetings/guestagendaitems GET with a body of tens to hundreds of MB (or a modest body with deeply nested arrays) delivered within the 5 s request timeout; :httpc buffers it whole and :json.decode materializes it as terms. The mediator's 15 s timeout abandons the call but does not stop the connector's Task, which keeps allocating; a hostile meeting window makes every search fetch such payloads again.",
              "preconditions": [
                "Hostile or compromised risapi1.komuna.net (or a hostile host passed via --base-url) able to push a multi-hundred-MB or deeply nested JSON body within the 5 s per-request timeout"
              ],
              "category": "Uncontrolled Resource Consumption",
              "severity": "LOW",
              "confidence": "medium",
              "recommendation": "Enforce a maximum accepted body size (abort above a fixed byte budget, or stream with a cap) and a JSON nesting-depth limit before decoding; cap the sizes of individual fields (textblocks.content) that later stages process.",
              "cwe_id": "CWE-400",
              "snippet": "{:ok, :json.decode(body)}",
              "symbol": "KomkiConnectorRis.Http.decode/1",
              "declared_line": 96,
              "claudeSecurityPluginFindingId": "v3:c49e6505985b58906bd94bfac68394c0d2f781a4503e76d0e2e53bc228896350",
