        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-276",
          "ruleIndex": 6,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Confidential room-document store created with default world-readable permissions (no mode hardening, unlike the sibling run dirs).\n\nensure_run_dirs! explicitly chmods <base>/run and <base>/run/connectors to 0700 two lines above, but creates the documents connector's entire read scope — the store of label-controlled room documents, which even the mediator is sandboxed from reading (mediator_profile.ex:77-85 allows only metadata) — with a bare mkdir_p! (default 0777 & ~umask = 0755); intake (session_intake.ex:253) and mediator templates (templates.ex:498-499) do the same, staged files inherit their source mode via File.cp (typically 0644; verified copy_file_mode in Elixir 1.19.5/1.20.4) and template documents are File.write! (0644). No chmod of documents_dir, its mediator parent, or the base exists anywhere in the codebase, so any other local account that can traverse the base reads every room document and lists their ids, bypassing the Gate/label architecture entirely. The data flow leads out of the component (komki_connector_documents reads this dir via --documents-dir) into the CLI launcher that provisions it.\n\nImpact: Confidentiality of all admitted room documents (including vertraulich-labeled ones) and their document ids to any other local account able to traverse the komki base — the OS permission layer is the only enforcement for non-komki processes, and the seatbelt profiles constrain only komki's own processes.\n\nExploit scenario: On a shared/Linux host with a traversable home (or a komki base outside the home), a second local user lists <base>/mediator/documents and reads the Fraktionsraum documents directly, no Gate, no connector, no token.\n\nPreconditions: Multi-user host, or a komki base outside a parent that other accounts cannot traverse (macOS home ACLs shield the common default); Default umask (022): directory 0755, staged/template files 0644.\n\nRecommendation: chmod documents_dir (and the mediator parent) to 0700 alongside run/connectors in ensure_run_dirs!, session_intake.plan and Templates.write_templates, and write staged and template documents with 0600 (File.cp already inherits source mode — force it), mirroring the treatment of sockets, tokens and the denials directory.\n\nCWE-276. Severity LOW, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "apps/komki_cli/lib/komki_cli/connectors.ex",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 345,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "    File.mkdir_p!(documents_dir(cfg))"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "KomkiCli.Connectors.ensure_run_dirs!/1",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "KomkiCli.Connectors.ensure_run_dirs!/1"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "claudeSecurityPlugin": {
              "id": "F30",
              "title": "Confidential room-document store created with default world-readable permissions (no mode hardening, unlike the sibling run dirs)",
              "impact": "Confidentiality of all admitted room documents (including vertraulich-labeled ones) and their document ids to any other local account able to traverse the komki base — the OS permission layer is the only enforcement for non-komki processes, and the seatbelt profiles constrain only komki's own processes.",
              "file": "apps/komki_cli/lib/komki_cli/connectors.ex",
              "line": 345,
              "description": "ensure_run_dirs! explicitly chmods <base>/run and <base>/run/connectors to 0700 two lines above, but creates the documents connector's entire read scope — the store of label-controlled room documents, which even the mediator is sandboxed from reading (mediator_profile.ex:77-85 allows only metadata) — with a bare mkdir_p! (default 0777 & ~umask = 0755); intake (session_intake.ex:253) and mediator templates (templates.ex:498-499) do the same, staged files inherit their source mode via File.cp (typically 0644; verified copy_file_mode in Elixir 1.19.5/1.20.4) and template documents are File.write! (0644). No chmod of documents_dir, its mediator parent, or the base exists anywhere in the codebase, so any other local account that can traverse the base reads every room document and lists their ids, bypassing the Gate/label architecture entirely. The data flow leads out of the component (komki_connector_documents reads this dir via --documents-dir) into the CLI launcher that provisions it.",
              "exploit_scenario": "On a shared/Linux host with a traversable home (or a komki base outside the home), a second local user lists <base>/mediator/documents and reads the Fraktionsraum documents directly, no Gate, no connector, no token.",
              "preconditions": [
