        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-74",
          "ruleIndex": 16,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Terminal control-sequence injection via unsanitized filesystem-derived CLI output.\n\nThe session-intake header writes user-chosen file paths to the terminal byte-for-byte (`IO.write`), while `KomkiCli.Terminal.sanitize/1` is applied only to pi stdout — so escape bytes and newlines in an attacker-influenced file name reach the victim's terminal verbatim, the exact harm class the project documents and defends against for model output (OSC 52 clipboard write, OSC 8, CSI line overwrite).\n\nImpact: Display forgery of a human decision surface (a file named with embedded newlines can inject fake 'datei: … permit' lines into the intake preview), terminal-title/clipboard manipulation in terminals honoring OSC 52. The same sink class exists for error reasons (render {:error,…} embeds raw paths, e.g. '--gguf-from Pfad nicht gefunden: <path>') and the denial footer at cli.ex:993, whose verbatim-path rule (denials.ex @verbatim_prefixes) passes model/attacker-influenced path bytes under /usr, /opt, … through raw.\n\nExploit scenario: A victim receives a document whose name contains '\\n  datei: vertraulich.md -> permit' or an OSC 52 sequence (valid APFS file names), and brings it into 'komki session <file>'; the intake header prints the crafted lines/sequences to the terminal, misrepresenting what is being admitted or overwriting the clipboard.\n\nPreconditions: Victim selects an attacker-named file (or attacker-influenced config path / sandbox-denial target) in a komki command; For clipboard exfil: terminal emulator honors OSC 52; plain display forgery via newline/CSI bytes works universally.\n\nRecommendation: Route every terminal-bound string built from filesystem or log data through KomkiCli.Terminal.sanitize/1 — session headers, StartContract.header values, error reasons, and the denial footer — exactly as render({:run_ok,…}) already does for pi output.\n\nCWE-74. Severity LOW, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "apps/komki_cli/lib/komki_cli/cli.ex",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 610,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "        if header != [], do: IO.write(Enum.join(header, \"\\n\") <> \"\\n\")"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "run_session/1",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "run_session/1"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
