        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-863",
          "ruleIndex": 1,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "`komki journal verify` executes the pinned mediator program without the pin gate that up/run/session enforce.\n\njournal_verify runs the program recorded at cfg.mediator_bin (under the escript runtime, or the Burrito binary at line 1075) unsandboxed and without comparing its bytes to the recorded pin, although the pin gate (steps.ex:631 Pins.checks, gating `up` at steps.ex:1007 and the full doctor for run/session) exists precisely to stop komki from executing a program silently swapped at a pinned path; the swapped program's output is then rendered to the user as the journal verification verdict.\n\nImpact: A mediator binary silently swapped at its pinned path — the exact event the pin scheme detects — executes with the user's full privileges inside a komki command, and its stdout is presented as a genuine integrity verdict for the PDR audit journal, giving the user a forged \"Journal ok\" for a tampered trail.\n\nExploit scenario: A same-uid attacker (or compromised dependency) replaces the pinned komki-mediator file after tampering with the mediator journal. `komki up` and `komki doctor` refuse on the pin FAIL, but the user's routine `komki journal verify` executes the swapped binary, which prints a valid-looking verification result that komki renders as \"Journal ok\", laundering the tampered audit trail.\n\nPreconditions: Same-uid write access to the pinned mediator path (and/or the escript runtime path) on the instance; The user runs `komki journal verify` while the pins are drifted.\n\nRecommendation: Run the pin check (Pins.checks, or the cheap doctor_quick) before executing the mediator for journal verification and refuse on drift, mirroring the up/run/session gate; alternatively verify the mediator pin inside `journal_verify/0` before the System.cmd.\n\nCWE-863. Severity LOW, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "apps/komki_cli/lib/komki_cli/steps.ex",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1083,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "System.cmd(cfg.escript_bin, [cfg.mediator_bin | args], stderr_to_stdout: true)"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "KomkiCli.Steps.journal_verify/0",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "KomkiCli.Steps.journal_verify/0"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "claudeSecurityPlugin": {
              "id": "F32",
              "title": "`komki journal verify` executes the pinned mediator program without the pin gate that up/run/session enforce",
              "impact": "A mediator binary silently swapped at its pinned path — the exact event the pin scheme detects — executes with the user's full privileges inside a komki command, and its stdout is presented as a genuine integrity verdict for the PDR audit journal, giving the user a forged \"Journal ok\" for a tampered trail.",
              "file": "apps/komki_cli/lib/komki_cli/steps.ex",
