        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-732",
          "ruleIndex": 4,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Security-model registry.db (and instance policy files) created with default world-readable permissions, unlike every hardened sibling artifact.\n\nThe authoritative label registry is created by `Sqlite3.open(db_path)` with SQLite's default 0644 (umask-adjusted) inside directories made by `File.mkdir_p!` (0755), and no chmod is ever applied — while the same codebase explicitly hardens every sibling secret it considers locally sensitive: mediator.token 0600 and run/ 0700 (channel.ex:75,80), denials/ 0700 with 0600 reports (denials.ex:448-481), llama API key 0600 (llama.ex:160). Any other local OS user who can traverse the instance path can read the store. The same default-permission gap covers `<base>/mediator/room.json` (start contract: auftrag, verantwortliche_person, eingangsrechte) and `<base>/mediator/registry.json` (the Γ policy basis) written by Gamma.sync/Room.write_json.\n\nImpact: Read-only disclosure of the classification registry — bindings, reader circles, observer model, content_refs, and the append-only decision history including free-text `basis` justifications and `decided_by` attributions — plus the Γ export and the start contract, to other local users. No write/replace access: instance directories are owner-only writable and sticky-bit directories (e.g. /private/tmp) prevent file swapping.\n\nExploit scenario: The user sets KOMKI_HOME=/private/tmp/komki-test — the exact location komki's own error text suggests for short socket paths (channel.ex:67) and which the project's smoke-test workflow uses. A second local account on the machine traverses the 0755 directory chain and reads registry.db (0644) and mediator/room.json (0644), obtaining the security model, the human's classification decisions with their free-text justifications, and the confidential mandate ('auftrag') of the working room.\n\nPreconditions: A second local OS user account on the machine; Instance base on a path traversable by that user: any custom KOMKI_HOME outside the protected home (komki itself suggests /private/tmp/komki-test); for the default ~/.local/share/komki location this additionally depends on the macOS home-directory ACL denying traversal.\n\nRecommendation: Apply the same hardening the codebase already uses for token/denials/key: chmod registry.db to 0600 in with_conn/2 after creation (and consider 0700 for <base> and <base>/mediator, 0600 for room.json/registry.json), or create the whole instance tree under a restrictive umask so the policy model and decision records are not world-readable.\n\nCWE-732. Severity LOW, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "apps/komki_cli/lib/komki_cli/label_store.ex",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1242,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "    case Sqlite3.open(db_path) do"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "KomkiCli.LabelStore.with_conn/2",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "KomkiCli.LabelStore.with_conn/2"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "claudeSecurityPlugin": {
