              "description": "The authoritative label registry is created by `Sqlite3.open(db_path)` with SQLite's default 0644 (umask-adjusted) inside directories made by `File.mkdir_p!` (0755), and no chmod is ever applied — while the same codebase explicitly hardens every sibling secret it considers locally sensitive: mediator.token 0600 and run/ 0700 (channel.ex:75,80), denials/ 0700 with 0600 reports (denials.ex:448-481), llama API key 0600 (llama.ex:160). Any other local OS user who can traverse the instance path can read the store. The same default-permission gap covers `<base>/mediator/room.json` (start contract: auftrag, verantwortliche_person, eingangsrechte) and `<base>/mediator/registry.json` (the Γ policy basis) written by Gamma.sync/Room.write_json.",
              "exploit_scenario": "The user sets KOMKI_HOME=/private/tmp/komki-test — the exact location komki's own error text suggests for short socket paths (channel.ex:67) and which the project's smoke-test workflow uses. A second local account on the machine traverses the 0755 directory chain and reads registry.db (0644) and mediator/room.json (0644), obtaining the security model, the human's classification decisions with their free-text justifications, and the confidential mandate ('auftrag') of the working room.",
