        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-276",
          "ruleIndex": 6,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Registry-DB with classification decisions and content references is created with default (other-user readable) permissions.\n\nThe SQLite registry at ~/.local/share/komki/registry.db (default) holds the security model's bindings, decider names, free-text decision bases and content_refs (the CLI's --content-ref explicitly accepts a raw file path to a confidential document), but Sqlite3.open creates the file with SQLite's default umask-based mode (typically 0644) and no code in the store ever hardens it — unlike every sibling artifact the same codebase protects with 0600/0700 (mediator.token, llama.key, connector tokens, denial reports).\n\nImpact: Another local OS user can read the classification policy (who may read what, relaxation authorities), personal decision attribution (decided_by), free-text bases and document content_refs of non-public council material. Confidentiality of metadata only; no content and no credentials.\n\nExploit scenario: On a shared Mac, a second local account traverses /Users/<user>/.local/share/komki (parent dirs created 0755 by File.mkdir_p!, stock macOS home is traversable) and reads registry.db at mode 0644, learning which quarantined documents exist, their referenced paths, who classified them and why.\n\nPreconditions: Multi-user host: a second local account able to traverse the user's home (stock macOS default 0755); Default umask 022 so SQLite creates the DB world/other-readable; Instance uses the default base (KOMKI_HOME unset) and nobody has manually hardened the file.\n\nRecommendation: Mirror the codebase's own pattern (channel.ex:77-81, llama.ex:157-161): on first creation, touch the DB path exclusively, File.chmod!(db_path, 0o600) before/after Sqlite3.open, and consider 0700 for the base directory; do the same for the -wal/-shm companion files.\n\nCWE-276. Severity LOW, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "apps/komki_cli/lib/komki_cli/label_store.ex",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1242,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "    case Sqlite3.open(db_path) do"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "KomkiCli.LabelStore.with_conn/2",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "KomkiCli.LabelStore.with_conn/2"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "claudeSecurityPlugin": {
              "id": "F34",
              "title": "Registry-DB with classification decisions and content references is created with default (other-user readable) permissions",
              "impact": "Another local OS user can read the classification policy (who may read what, relaxation authorities), personal decision attribution (decided_by), free-text bases and document content_refs of non-public council material. Confidentiality of metadata only; no content and no credentials.",
