              "description": "The SQLite registry at ~/.local/share/komki/registry.db (default) holds the security model's bindings, decider names, free-text decision bases and content_refs (the CLI's --content-ref explicitly accepts a raw file path to a confidential document), but Sqlite3.open creates the file with SQLite's default umask-based mode (typically 0644) and no code in the store ever hardens it — unlike every sibling artifact the same codebase protects with 0600/0700 (mediator.token, llama.key, connector tokens, denial reports).",
              "exploit_scenario": "On a shared Mac, a second local account traverses /Users/<user>/.local/share/komki (parent dirs created 0755 by File.mkdir_p!, stock macOS home is traversable) and reads registry.db at mode 0644, learning which quarantined documents exist, their referenced paths, who classified them and why.",
              "preconditions": [
